# make tablet-smoke, its Qt half (W22-S05): qtdemo on go.img with the Qt
# disk and QEMU's tablet; qt.env gives Qt's evdev mouse handler event2 with
# "abs". No corner first: the tablet puts the pointer on the Add button
# (529,125) and the File menu (21,12) wherever it was.
wait burrow>
screen 1024 768
type run /opt/qt/bin/qtdemo
key ret
wait qtdemo: ready
type hello burrow
wait typed "hello burrow"
abs 900 600
sleep 1
abs 529 125
sleep 1
click left
wait added "hello burrow"
abs 21 12
sleep 1
click left
wait menu open
key esc
wait menu closed
key ctrl-q
wait qtdemo: quit
wait burrow>
type poweroff
key ret
